L0240: Use after move

A non-Copy value was consumed by an earlier operation or a previous loop iteration. Runtime argument evaluation still consumes values even when the outer result is erased. Borrow, explicitly clone a cloneable value, or restructure ownership so each move has a live source.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/moved_in_loop.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// A value declared outside a loop and moved in its body is gone when the
// next pass reaches the move, unless it is assigned again before the end of
// the body or a `continue`: rustc's E0382, reported at the move.
struct Token {
    id: u8,
}

fn consume(t: Token) -> u8 {
    t.id
}

fn every_pass(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let t = Token { id: 1 };
    let mut total = 0u8;
    for i in 0..n {
        total = total.wrapping_add(consume(t));
    }
    total
}

// Assigned again on one path only: the `continue` leaves it moved.
fn skipped(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let mut t = Token { id: 1 };
    let mut total = 0u8;
    let mut i = 0u8;
    while i < n {
        i = i.wrapping_add(1);
        total = total.wrapping_add(consume(t));
        if total > 10 {
            continue;
        } else {
            t = Token { id: i };
        }
    }
    total
}
```

Language, as built: [1.13:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.13:1).
